$post_body = <<<'HTML'
<p>Most window blinds last 7-10 years. High-quality materials in low-humidity rooms can stretch that to 12 years or longer. Cheap vinyl in a sunny kitchen might start failing in three to four.</p>
<p>This guide covers specific lifespan data by material and what the main variables are. For guidance on which material suits each room type before you order, our window blind material guide covers room-by-room recommendations.</p>
%IMAGE1%
<h2 id="average-lifespan-by-blind-type">Average Lifespan by Blind Type</h2>
<p>Here's a practical breakdown by material and product type under normal residential conditions.</p>
<ul class="bp-list">
  <li><strong>Faux wood horizontal blinds:</strong> 7-10 years in most rooms. Better in dry conditions, shorter in high humidity.</li>
  <li><strong>Aluminum horizontal blinds:</strong> 7-10 years in low-traffic rooms. Bend and dent more easily under heavy use.</li>
  <li><strong>Real wood blinds:</strong> 5-8 years in rooms without humidity issues. Shorter in bathrooms or kitchens.</li>
</ul>
<p>Vertical blinds (fabric or vinyl): 5-8 years. Individual slats tangle and break, reducing function before the product itself wears out.</p>
<p>Plantation shutters: 20-25 years or more. The most durable residential window treatment.</p>
<p>Our <a href="%BASE%/window-treatments/window-blinds/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">window blinds</a> hub covers all the blind types we carry if you're comparing options for a replacement.</p>
<h2 id="what-makes-blinds-age-faster-than-they-should">What Makes Blinds Age Faster Than They Should?</h2>
<p>UV exposure, high humidity, and rough handling are the three main reasons blinds fail early. A west-facing window with afternoon sun hitting the same spot every day degrades slat finishes and fades colors over two to three years. A bathroom without proper ventilation adds moisture every day, and wood and vinyl respond by warping or becoming brittle.</p>
<p>Pulling the cord at an angle instead of straight down is the most common source of mechanism failure. The tilting rod and the cord lock take uneven stress and break years before the slats themselves need replacing.</p>
<h2 id="signs-your-window-blinds-need-replacing">Signs Your Window Blinds Need Replacing</h2>
<p>Yellowing or discoloration is usually the first visible sign. In vinyl blinds it means the material is breaking down. In painted blinds it means the finish is failing.</p>
<p>Warping, where the slats curve or bow when closed, means the material has absorbed enough moisture or UV damage that it won't recover. A warped slat doesn't close flat and lets light through.</p>
<p>Broken slats, tangled cords, and tilt mechanisms that no longer hold position are signs the product has reached the end of its practical life, even if it still looks acceptable from across the room.</p>
<p>If more than two or three slats are broken, or the cord has snapped at the lock, replacement is usually more cost-effective than repair.</p>
<h2 id="how-to-get-more-years-from-your-current-blinds">How to Get More Years From Your Current Blinds?</h2>
<p>Regular light dusting prevents buildup that works into the tilting mechanism. Pulling the cord straight down rather than at an angle extends the life of the cord lock. Keeping bathroom and kitchen humidity down, either with ventilation or a range hood, reduces moisture exposure to the slats.</p>
<p>Our <a href="%BASE%/guidelines/care-and-maintenance/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">care and maintenance guide</a> covers specific cleaning methods by material and the handling habits that extend blind life.</p>
<h2 id="when-to-replace-vs-repair-window-blinds-in-aurora-il">When to Replace vs. Repair Window Blinds in Aurora, IL</h2>
<p>Single cord or tilt issues are worth looking at for repair if the slats are still in good condition. A cord replacement or a new tilt rod is less expensive than a full product replacement.</p>
<p>Warping, yellowing, or widespread slat damage means replacement is the right answer. Partial repairs on a product that's already past its best leave you with a product that fails again soon.</p>
<p>Our <a href="%BASE%/guidelines/professional-installation/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">professional installation guide</a> explains what a correct installation looks like and what to check when evaluating whether your current blinds were installed correctly.</p>
%IMAGE2%
<h2 id="blind-replacement-in-aurora-il">Blind Replacement in Aurora, IL</h2>
<p>Creative Blinds and Drapes handles blind replacement and new installation in Aurora, IL and surrounding communities. We come to your home, measure the windows correctly, and install the new product ourselves.</p>
<p>See our full horizontal blind options on our <a href="%BASE%/window-treatments/window-blinds/horizontal-blinds/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">horizontal blinds page</a> or contact us to book a free in-home visit.</p>
